 members of Parliament rather than as Ministers, and do not necessarily support the government position.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSixth National Government of New Zealand (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sixth_National_Government_of_New_Zealand)\nciteturn20search23 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Seymour also opined that ACT as the second largest party in the coalition should hold the position of Deputy Prime Minister and have more ministerial portfolios than NZ First. That same day, the three parties entered into talks about allocating cabinet ministerial positions. ... The Government plan gained support from the New Zealand Taxpayers' Union. ... The Government also conceded its policy to dissolve Te Aka Whai Ora had been motivated by political expediency during the 2023 election campaign. ... *  \"Government in caretaker mode as coalition talks start\". ... \"National, Act, NZ First coalition talks: Winston Peters blames delayed negotiations on decision supported by...\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBasic Law for the Federal Republic of Germany (https://www.gesetze-im-internet.de/englisch_gg/englisch_gg.html)\nciteturn20view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.gesetze-im-internet.de/englisch_gg/englisch_gg.html\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 2115\nL0: Übersetzung durch Professor Christian Tomuschat, Professor David P. Currie, Professor Donald P. Kommers und Raymond Kerr, in Kooperation mit dem Sprachendienst des Deutschen Bundestages\nL1: \nL2: Translated by Professor Christian Tomuschat, Professor David P. Currie, Professor Donald P. Kommers and Raymond Kerr, in cooperation with the Language Service of the German Bundestag\nL3: \nL4: Stand: Die Übersetzung berücksichtigt die Änderung(en) des Gesetzes durch Artikel 1 des Gesetzes vom 22. März 2025 (BGBl. 2025 I Nr. 94)\n-----------------